'''''Breutelia chrysocoma''''', also known as the '''bottle brush moss'''<ref name=iucn/> and the '''golden-head moss''',<ref name=GBIF/> is a species of moss in the [[Bartramiaceae]] family. It is an attractive and conspicuous moss found most commonly in the north Atlantic, with strongholds in western Britain, Ireland and western Norway.<ref name=GBIF>{{GBIF |title=''Breutelia chrysocoma'' (Hedw.) Lindb. |id=2676330 |access-date=2025-01-09}}</ref> Other populations have been found across western and central Europe but far less common compared to the hyper-oceanic zone of northwest Europe. It is most commonly found on upland acidic grassland, especially near flushes.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Breutelia chrysocoma |url=https://www.britishbryologicalsociety.org.uk/learning/species-finder/breutelia-chrysocoma/ |access-date=2025-01-09 |website=British Bryological Society |language=en-GB}}</ref>

